{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_14","type":"agent_message","text":"CodeGraph says it collects only a narrow set of anonymous usage telemetry: install/uninstall events, coarse index stats such as languages plus bucketed file counts/durations, and daily aggregated tool/command usage with agent name/version, alongside a random machine UUID and basic platform metadata. It explicitly guarantees it does **not** collect source code, file paths or names, repo names/URLs, symbol names, search queries, IP addresses, geolocation, fingerprints, usernames, hostnames, emails, or environment variables, and if telemetry is turned off it records nothing and sends no network traffic at all. Sources: [TELEMETRY.md](https://github.com/colbymchenry/codegraph/blob/main/TELEMETRY.md), [telemetry-worker mention in same doc](https://github.com/colbymchenry/codegraph/blob/main/TELEMETRY.md)."}}
